  "question": {
    "text": "In the electrolysis of alumina to obtain aluminium metal, cryolite is added mainly to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "y4acA",
      "text": "\nlower the melting point of alumina\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "j3FSl",
      "text": "\ndissolve alumina in molten cryolite\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aQs0P",
      "text": "\nremove the impurities of alumina\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ImNeD",
      "text": "\nincrease the electrical conductivity",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Fused alumina $\\left(\\mathrm{Al}_2 \\mathrm{O}_3\\right)$ is a bad conductor of electricity. Therefore, cryolite $\\left(\\mathrm{Na}_3 \\mathrm{AlF}_6\\right)$ and fluorspar $\\left(\\mathrm{CaF}_2\\right)$ are added to purified alumina which not only make alumina a good conductor of electricity but also reduce the melting point of the mixture to around $1140 \\mathrm{~K}$.",
    "image": null
  },
